{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A1NKnCujgtGc7TN9nqbr1j","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target units bpm %lthr garmin export zone\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157\"},{\"title\":\"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725\"},{\"title\":\"Incorrect structured workout rendering in calendar export\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/incorrect-structured-workout-rendering-in-calendar-export/127096\"},{\"title\":\"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range\"},{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu and Garmin sync for right intensities\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-and-garmin-sync-for-right-intensities/59698\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Running Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/213d5f7b06df7793bfdba7feb49869bae4075379/src/resources/run-workout-syntax.md\"},{\"title\":\"Running Workout Builder\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/running-workout-builder/5805\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521?page=9\"},{\"title\":\"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/need-help-with-hr-based-workouts-in-bpm/120685\"}]\n\nThe search turned up mostly Intervals.icu forum threads, not official documentation, so treat these as user reports.\n\n- **Units in workouts:** Intervals.icu workouts can set HR targets as a percentage of LTHR, and the rendered workout text adds the bpm range computed from the athlete's LTHR. One user found that typing bpm ranges directly into the editor did not work for them. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Incorrect structured workout rendering in calendar export\")\n- **Garmin export:** One forum user believed targets are sent to Garmin as a percentage of LTHR, so a mismatch in LTHR between the two apps produces the wrong bpm range. Another user saw a 100 bpm offset on a Garmin-built workout. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\")\n- **Garmin bug workaround:** The developer added a workaround that, for Garmin-manufacturer files only, skips subtracting 100 from custom HR range high ends at or below 80 (when none are 250 or higher). (same thread, later page)\n- **Zones:** Zone-based targets appear in the JSON as an hr_zone value, with no zone boundaries included. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range\")\n- **HR zones on the watch:** Intervals.icu cannot change Garmin Connect settings, so HR zones and LTHR must be set manually on both platforms to match. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Intervals.icu and Garmin sync for right intensities\")\n- **%HRR:** Intervals.icu has no native %HRR (Karvonen) zone option as of the feature request; users work around it with custom zones built from LTHR percentages. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Native Heart Rate Reserve…\")\n- **Absolute bpm targets:** A thread on building fixed 130–140 bpm workouts had no clear answer on how Intervals.icu communicates bpm targets to Garmin. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)\")\n\nI didn't find official Intervals.icu documentation on the exact export encoding for HR targets. Checking a Garmin FIT file's workout structure or the Intervals.icu API docs would confirm how units are encoded.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06edac73-5082-442a-989c-48a8b19b4364","uuid":"cdb0e588-659a-4d5d-a569-673e655d1c74","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:03:43.131Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target units bpm %lthr garmin export zone","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01RKbGojWjqwQy43EshaTrr4","content":[{"title":"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356"},{"title":"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157"},{"title":"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725"},{"title":"Incorrect structured workout rendering in calendar export","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/incorrect-structured-workout-rendering-in-calendar-export/127096"},{"title":"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range"},{"title":"Intervals.icu and Garmin sync for right intensities","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-and-garmin-sync-for-right-intensities/59698"},{"title":"# Intervals.icu Running Workout Syntax","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/213d5f7b06df7793bfdba7feb49869bae4075379/src/resources/run-workout-syntax.md"},{"title":"Running Workout Builder","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/running-workout-builder/5805"},{"title":"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521?page=9"},{"title":"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/need-help-with-hr-based-workouts-in-bpm/120685"}]},"The search turned up mostly Intervals.icu forum threads, not official documentation, so treat these as user reports.\n\n- **Units in workouts:** Intervals.icu workouts can set HR targets as a percentage of LTHR, and the rendered workout text adds the bpm range computed from the athlete's LTHR. One user found that typing bpm ranges directly into the editor did not work for them. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Incorrect structured workout rendering in calendar export\")\n- **Garmin export:** One forum user believed targets are sent to Garmin as a percentage of LTHR, so a mismatch in LTHR between the two apps produces the wrong bpm range. Another user saw a 100 bpm offset on a Garmin-built workout. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\")\n- **Garmin bug workaround:** The developer added a workaround that, for Garmin-manufacturer files only, skips subtracting 100 from custom HR range high ends at or below 80 (when none are 250 or higher). (same thread, later page)\n- **Zones:** Zone-based targets appear in the JSON as an hr_zone value, with no zone boundaries included. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range\")\n- **HR zones on the watch:** Intervals.icu cannot change Garmin Connect settings, so HR zones and LTHR must be set manually on both platforms to match. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Intervals.icu and Garmin sync for right intensities\")\n- **%HRR:** Intervals.icu has no native %HRR (Karvonen) zone option as of the feature request; users work around it with custom zones built from LTHR percentages. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Native Heart Rate Reserve…\")\n- **Absolute bpm targets:** A thread on building fixed 130–140 bpm workouts had no clear answer on how Intervals.icu communicates bpm targets to Garmin. (forum.intervals.icu, \"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)\")\n\nI didn't find official Intervals.icu documentation on the exact export encoding for HR targets. Checking a Garmin FIT file's workout structure or the Intervals.icu API docs would confirm how units are encoded."],"durationSeconds":7.884928292000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01A1NKnCujgtGc7TN9nqbr1j","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
